    "created_at": "2025-08-08T09:29:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-08-08T09:29:05Z",
    "body": "> Is there any reason something other than `undefined` is allowed in a `setter` operation?\n\n`SpecialOperation` probably made more sense when there were more things that [actually returned something](https://www.w3.org/TR/2010/WD-WebIDL-20101021/#idl-special-operations), but given it's only the getter returning something now, time to break down this syntax.",
